    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d240">

                <pb facs="0569" n="485" sameAs="frus:frus1886/pg485"/>

                <head>No. 236.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Sir L. West to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1886-12-07"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 7, 1886</date>.
                        (Received December 9.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to your note of the 30th of
                    July last, I am instructed by the Earl of Iddesleigh to communicate to you the
                    inclosed copy of a dispatch, with its inclosures, from the officer administering
                    the Government of Canada, respecting the action of the customs officer at
                    Magdalen Islands, in the case of the United States fishing vessel Mascotte.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>L. S. SACKVILLE WEST.</signed></closer>





